  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Water Security and Resilience in FCDO Partnerships: Harnessing Indicators for Action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AGWA will lead a team of experts and partners to evaluate, expand, and align FCDO indicators for both water and climate resilience specific to the context of water security programming. AGWA will recommend a set of performance indicators that co-measure water and climate security, such as by looking at risk assessment, climate preparation and coordination, and system-level reliability and change, including both social, infrastructure, and eco-hydrological variables.
The indicators will focus on meaningful and cost-viable impacts designed to demonstrate strengthened resilience through water management, which will be defined as water resilience of citizens, households, communities, corporations/farms/factories, investors/investments, and governments/countries. This will support the ability to track and monitor systemic change along a spectrum of water resilience and identify indicators linked to the most significant instances of change.
While we will develop a basket of indicators to track water and climate security over timescales relevant for this body of work, we anticipate a broad range of categories.</narrative>
  </description>
